/-!
# VIII09 — the actual cubic response `c_j`, `d_j`

The task-book construction is

  `c_j = bfun 0 q3_j`,  `d_j = vfun 0 q3_j r3_j`

i.e. the accepted VIII08/R solver is called with **cubic solver parameter `j3 = 0`** and the
physical source pair `(q3_j, r3_j)`.  The parameter of that solver is the angular-momentum
coefficient *of the order being solved*, and there is no `ε³` angular parameter in the test
family (`J_ε = ε j`), so the call is `0`; the physical `j` enters only through the source.

This file instantiates `viii08_main` with the source budgets `Aq = |j|³`, `Ar = 2|j|³` and reads off:

* `MagClass 3 c_j`, `VClass 3 d_j`, both source equations and pair uniqueness;
* the four response bounds `|R c_j| ≤ |j|³/8`, `|R² c_j'| ≤ |j|³`,
  `|R³ d_j| ≤ 11|j|³/12`, `|R⁴ d_j'| ≤ 11|j|³/4`;
* the four far-field limits with `σ3 = sigmaB 0 q3_j`.
-/

